# The review service (see worker/). It also keeps the clips a person shares as a link (README, Shared clips).
# Leave empty to keep the app local-only: nothing is then sent anywhere, and there is no share link.
VITE_REVIEW_API_URL=
# Sent as a bearer token with every upload. It ships in the bundle, so it is not a secret: it only keeps strangers from writing by accident.
VITE_REVIEW_INGEST_TOKEN=
# Public folder that holds the pose models, the wasm runtimes and the sample videos: <review Worker URL>/assets, an R2 bucket (layout:
# scripts/assets-upload.mjs, filled by `make assets-upload`). Set: the build leaves those files out and the app reads them from there.
# Empty: they are served from this origin (`npm run fetch-assets`), and there is no sample. Keep it empty for `npm run dev` and the
# headless runs, which then read public/ instead of downloading every model again.
VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL=
# Only for `make assets-upload` / `asset-remove` / `assets-remove` (R2's S3 API): Cloudflare dashboard > R2 > Manage API tokens, an
# "Object Read & Write" token on the bucket trampovision-assets. Never in the bundle (no VITE_ prefix), never in the Vercel project.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Jev (TypeSafe), the Classification tab of the coach rail (advanced tools). Set to /api/jev: the tab then calls the Vercel function api/jev/systemone.ts,
# same origin, so the CSP and the local-only guard are unchanged. Empty: the tab says Jev is not in this build.
VITE_JEV_API_URL=
# The Jev key, read by that function (a secret of the Vercel project, no VITE_ prefix: it never reaches the bundle). Also used by `make jev-eval`.
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
